Author: lonewolf-jp <lonewolf-jp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Nov 12 01:48:35 2026 +0900

    feat(isr): stamp retire entries with their domain and aggregate latency per domain
    
    Retire latency was measured for the whole engine, so an EQ-domain delay could
    not be separated from an ISR-domain one. Stamp every deletion entry with the
    domain that owns its retire queue, and report the three-way latency split per
    domain without changing the existing thresholds or pass/fail decision.
    
    - add RetireDomainId (Unstamped/Unknown/EngineISR/EQ) and stamp the entry in
      DeferredDeletionQueue::enqueue through the epoch provider instead of
      inferring the domain later from the thread or the entry type
    - make the epoch domain constructor argument mandatory for every build and
      record invalid assignments instead of silently accepting them
    - add firstScanTsNs and split the measured delay into driver / epoch-safe /
      execution segments, exposed as retireLatencyClassified next to the existing
      retireLatencyD1 fields
    - drive EQ-domain reclaim from the existing message-thread timer, and make the
      EQ processor skip state access when RCU entry fails
    - pass publish reasons explicitly and record teardown and world-lifetime
      measurements used by the same report
    - add DomainTagTests and update the EpochDomain construction sites
    
    Verified with a Release build and ctest (57/57 passed).

